Print It True: Letterpress Newspaper · Lemo-Opuscar

Picture
- Every page, rule, masthead, drop cap, halftone photograph, stamp, wire tape, slug and shadow is drawn in code (demo/main.js, demo/engine/*.js). The three "photographs" (smoke over a mill, a bakery chimney at dawn, a queue at a shop) are painted procedurally as grey-scale and printed as 45-degree dot screens; no photo, scan or stock image is used.
- The newspaper (The Tallow Bay Lantern), the town, the mill, the bakery, every headline, name, price and advertisement are invented. No real publication, person, firm, place, event or logo appears.

Fonts (SIL Open Font License 1.1; the files are copied into demo/fonts/ and are not committed)
- EB Garamond (roman and italic, variable), Georg Duffner and Octavio Pardo, https://github.com/google/fonts/tree/main/ofl/ebgaramond (headlines, deck, small heads; licence: demo/fonts/OFL-EBGaramond.txt)
- Cormorant Garamond (variable), Christian Thalmann (Catharsis Fonts), https://github.com/google/fonts/tree/main/ofl/cormorantgaramond (masthead)
- IM FELL English (roman and italic), Igino Marini, from core/fonts/ (body copy and captions; licence: demo/fonts/OFL-core-fonts.md)
- Courier Prime Bold, Quote-Unquote Apps, https://fonts.google.com/specimen/Courier+Prime (datelines, stamps, wire tape)

Voice
- Kokoro TTS v1.0 (hexgrad/Kokoro-82M, Apache-2.0), voice bm_fable, via kokoro-onnx
- Speech check only (not in the film): faster-whisper / OpenAI Whisper (MIT)

Music
- Original composition, synthesised in numpy (demo/mix.py): tine piano (additive plus FM bite), upright bass, brushes, a struck-bar bell. No samples.

Sound design
- Rotary press thrum, slug clack, line casting ticks, rules, paper slaps, stamps, telephone bell, telegraph key, halftone development ticks: all synthesised in numpy (demo/mix.py, core/audio/sfx.py). No recordings.
